  "problem_statement": "After the AES128 CMAC, HMAC-SHA1, and HMAC-SHA256 contexts are finalized, their key material and internal state must be securely cleared from memory. Currently, the key buffers and internal cipher contexts retain their values after the finalization step, which can expose sensitive data to memory inspection. A caller that finalizes these contexts must be able to verify that the relevant internal buffers and cipher contexts have been zeroed out.",
